   "text": {
    "L1": "A whole cut into ten equal parts gives tenths. One tenth is 0.1, or 1/10.",
    "L2": "Cut one tenth into ten equal parts. Each small part is one hundredth: 0.01, or 1/100.",
    "L3": "So ten hundredths make one tenth. The place value tells us how much each digit means.",
    "L4": "Here is a common mistake: 0.05 and 0.5 both have a five, but they are not equal.",
    "L5": "The zero in 0.05 holds the tenths place. Five hundredths is ten times smaller than five tenths.",
    "L6": "For example, 0.5 is 5/10, while 0.05 is 5/100. A grid makes the difference visible.",
    "L7": "A final example: 1 centimetre is 0.01 metre, so 7 centimetres is 0.07 metre. Therefore 2 metres 7 centimetres is 2.07 metres.",
    "L8": "Now check your understanding. Tap the decimal that means five hundredths."
   },
